# Private physiology and public illness projection

The private combined physiology takes a deterministic baseline, adds each
episode's private meter state, and adds intervention effects. Terminal status
checks each combined meter against its terminal threshold. The public illness
status writer instead derives symptomatic and critical flags from individual
episode stages when a notice is written. These are different inputs and update
mechanisms; this source read does not prove a supported state where a terminal
private meter passes every action or simulator readiness gate.

Qualify all condition inputs, public readiness call sites, notification and
intervention histories, and supported states before deciding the zero-preview
path's reachability. No runtime execution or product repair was performed.
